# Silence zoxide's "configuration issue" doctor banner. It fires on every
# non-interactive shell (e.g. Claude Code's Bash tool re-sources config per
# call), even though zoxide is already initialized correctly at the end of
# zshrc. Lives in .zshenv so it applies to non-interactive shells too.
export _ZO_DOCTOR=0

# ZSH_HUMAN_SHELL -- 1 when a person is driving this shell, 0 otherwise.
#
# Aliases that shadow standard commands (ls -> eza, cat -> bat, rm -> rm -i)
# are a convenience at a prompt and a hazard everywhere else. Coding agents
# shell out through this config expecting POSIX behavior, so `ls -la` becomes
# `eza --tree -la`, `rm -rf` blocks on a confirmation prompt, and a global
# alias like `G` rewrites a command line the agent never meant to change.
#
# Guard anything that shadows a real command with this flag. To teach it about
# another agent, add that agent's environment marker to the list below.
typeset -g ZSH_HUMAN_SHELL=0
if [[ -o interactive ]] &&
   [[ -z "${CLAUDECODE-}${CLAUDE_CODE_ENTRYPOINT-}${AI_AGENT-}${CURSOR_AGENT-}${CODEX_SANDBOX-}" ]]; then
  ZSH_HUMAN_SHELL=1
fi
